title: MikroTik Filesystem system disk
agents: mikrotik
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Usage of the system storage of a MikroTik RouterOS 6 or 7 device
 ({total-hdd-space} and {free-hdd-space} of {/system/resource}) with the
 standard filesystem check: levels, magic factor and trends via the rule
 {File systems (used space and growth)}, default {WARN} at 80%, {CRIT} at
 90%. NAND bad blocks are only shown in the details, they have their own
 service {NAND bad blocks}.

 On a host that is also polled via SNMP the agent section supersedes the
 SNMP section (hr_fs), so the service exists once. This only applies
 when the module delivered data.

 To connect to the MikroTik device a special datasource program is
 used: {MikroTik RouterOS} in Setup > Agents > Other integrations,
 module "System resources". The module is opt-in, "all" does not
 include it.

item:
 {system disk}, the same item as via SNMP.

perfdata:
 Used, free and total space, growth and trend.

inventory:
 One service.
